      "proposed_method": [
        {
          "name": "Minimal chiral electron-transfer assembly",
          "description": "Build a short coiled-coil peptide assembly that brings a donor and an acceptor to a fixed nanometer separation. Use identical sequences synthesized from L- or D-amino acids, with site-specific redox labels at defined positions. The assembly is a reduced model of protein-like chiral order relevant to electron transfer [Author et al., 2023](https://openalex.org/W4384627421), and peptides are chosen because homochiral peptide stability under aqueous conditions is a plausible prebiotic factor [Author et al., 2023](https://openalex.org/W4313574776)."
        },
        {
          "name": "One-factor chiral-uniformity perturbation",
          "description": "Vary only the enantiomeric uniformity of the assembly while holding sequence, length, total peptide concentration, label stoichiometry, ionic strength, pH, temperature, and surface density constant. The perturbation moves from all-L to racemic to all-D states, allowing comparison with system-level homochirality questions [Author et al., 2021](https://openalex.org/W3120596068) and avoiding reliance on a specialized amplification reaction such as the Soai system [Author et al., 2020](https://openalex.org/W3210500841)."
