          "name": "Fidelity and channel-capacity readout",
          "description": "Measure electron-transfer output as a conditional input-output channel. Inputs are controlled donor excitation or electrochemical potential states; outputs are acceptor charge-separation, fluorescence quenching, or current states. Estimate error rates and mutual information from replicate measurements. This adapts molecular-code models in which accuracy, diversity, and cost determine the evolution of coding schemes [Author et al., 2008](https://openalex.org/W2115810426), and treats chiral selection as an information-theoretic symmetry-breaking problem [Author et al., 2010](https://openalex.org/W2156278460)."
        },
        {
          "name": "Necessity-contingency decision model",
          "description": "Use the measured channel capacities to parameterize an accuracy-diversity-cost model that compares homochiral, racemic, and mixed-chirality states under different functional objectives such as maximum fidelity, maximum diversity, or minimum cost. The output is a quantitative criterion for whether chirality is required for a given definition of life-like function, rather than a universal assertion. This connects chemical emergence to functional necessity [Author et al., 2021](https://openalex.org/W3120596068) and prebiotic persistence [Author et al., 2023](https://openalex.org/W4313574776)."
